@startuml 11-seq-negotiation
!include _style.iuml
title Discovery and content negotiation

participant "Client" as c
participant "muppet disco\n(xtxp.link)" as gw
participant "Hosting muppet" as node

c -> gw : GET https://xtxp.link/{host}/{path}@{ref}\n(+ query signed by the client's key)
gw -> gw : which muppets host sessions\nof {host}/{path} that this key may see?
gw --> c : 303 → the hosting muppet\n(or a list of visible sessions)

alt WebSocket upgrade
  c -> node : upgrade to WebSocket
  node --> c : XTXP stream:\nYrs v1 updates in XTXP frames
else Accept: text/html
  c -> node : GET
  node --> c : rendered current state as HTML\n+ forms that POST edits\n+ link "open in native client" → xtxp://{host}/{path}@{ref}
end

note over gw
  The disco hosts nothing, and anyone can run one.
  It is a future milestone; until then a client
  goes straight to the hosting muppet.
end note

note over c, node
  {ref} is @origin (an ordinary website as it is now), @main,
  a session name, or a state vector. The last @ always starts the ref;
  a bare URL redirects to the default ref.
end note
@enduml
